\section{Materials and Methods}

\subsection{Structural Composite Fabrication}
The UHPFRC--basalt composite was cast using:
\begin{itemize}
    \item Matrix density: $\rho = \SI{2850}{\kilogram\per\cubic\meter}$.
    \item Water-to-binder ratio: $\text{w/b} = 0.16$.
    \item Fiber reinforcement: $2.5\%$ steel/basalt hybrid.
    \item Autoclave curing: \SI{48}{\hour} at \SI{90}{\celsius}.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Optical Transport Testing}
Polarization-maintaining fibers were tested using OTDR and single-photon counting modules
at $\lambda = \SI{1310}{\nano\meter}$ and $\SI{1550}{\nano\meter}$.

\subsection{Cryptographic Processor Evaluation}
The AES-256 / AE9-256 hardened ASIC was subjected to:
\begin{itemize}
    \item \SI{400}{\giga\bit\per\second} saturation load,
    \item EMI injection from \SI{1}{\giga\hertz} to \SI{10}{\giga\hertz},
    \item entropy measurement via NIST SP 800-90B methodology.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Biological Simulation Protocol}
The pathogen simulation engine executed $10^9$ mutation variables across $10^8$ cycles,
with real-time sensor feedback at \SI{12.4}{\giga\hertz} sampling.

